  "claim_boundary": "A permanent manifest derived under this development protocol may assert only that the exact admitted source-v5 public reader-text inventory was embedded once through the fixed embed_many.v1 call with the pinned offline BGE-M3 identity and persisted as one content-addressed table. Before the first embedding call or any validate-existing result, the source-v5 admission owner must run its read-only full semantic rebuild with externally supplied protocol and artifact identities and all frozen validation inputs. That upstream validator reads sealed inputs under its own owner. The embedding projection then reads only the typed public plan and forwards only allowlisted user_utterance/current_input strings to BGE; no sealed payload, label, condition truth, action branch, PE, credit, judge value, or public outcome value is forwarded. This is an information-flow boundary, not process independence. The table contains no fitted or invoked reader and reader_fit_count remains zero for this protocol and materialization. The public source-v5 texts become development-spent/transductive inputs after successful materialization and cannot be called unseen. The artifact does not qualify Readable, hand off theta, establish geometric reachability or PE-credit achievability, freeze or execute a campaign, verify runtime blinding or ordering, estimate any effect, authorize formal or unseen evidence, establish any of the four abilities, represent humans, or authorize production ACTIVE. Model-free validate-existing verifies admission, identities, public inventory, table structure, and manifest closure without invoking BGE; it does not claim numerical embedding reproducibility. Create-only file fsync and manifest-last ordering do not establish Windows directory-entry or power-loss durability."
